---
import '../components/lab.css';
---
<header>
  <div class="section">lab setup · 1 of 4</div>
  <h2>local prerequisites and the project</h2>
  <p class="sub">start on your own machine, on the CPU. this section stays up as a reference during the lab</p>
</header>
<div class="pre10">
  <div class="card bar-a need">
    <h3>you need</h3>
    <div class="it"><b>Python 3.12</b><span>from <a href="https://www.python.org/downloads/">python.org/downloads</a>. the macOS system python may be older</span></div>
    <div class="it"><b>clang in your terminal</b><span>check: <code>clang --version</code></span>
      <span class="os"><em>mac</em> <code>xcode-select --install</code> if it's missing</span>
      <span class="os"><em>windows</em> install <a href="https://github.com/llvm/llvm-project/releases">LLVM</a>, add its <code>bin</code> folder to PATH, reopen the terminal</span></div>
    <div class="it"><b>an editor</b><span>VS Code or similar</span></div>
    <div class="it"><b>CPU as the first device</b><span>tinygrad turns tensor code into C, and clang compiles it <span class="nw">(slide 7)</span></span></div>
    <div class="it"><b>tinygrad 0.14.0</b><span>pinned by <code>requirements.txt</code>: <code>tinygrad==0.14.0</code>. setup installs it for you</span></div>
  </div>
  <div class="card bar-n step proj">
    <h3>get the project</h3>
    <p>clone it:</p>
<pre class="sh">git clone https://github.com/rvfvn/transformer-training-lab.git
cd transformer-training-lab</pre>
    <p>or open the local copy you already have, and run everything from its top folder</p>
    <p class="muted small">configs/ · scripts/ · tests/ · check_configs.py · check_environment.py · requirements.txt · setup-mac.sh · setup-windows.bat</p>
  </div>
</div>
<div class="src">sources: <a href="https://github.com/rvfvn/transformer-training-lab/blob/main/README.md">[13]</a> <a href="https://github.com/rvfvn/transformer-training-lab">[14]</a></div>
<style>
  .pre10 { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 1.15fr 1fr; gap: 1.2em; font-size: .66em; width: 100%; align-items: start; }
  .need { display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: .35em; }
  .need h3, .proj h3 { color: var(--accent); }
  .it { display: block; padding-bottom: .3em; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border); }
  .it > b { margin-right: .4em; }
  .it > span { display: block; }
  /* the first line of each item sits beside its title, like slide 12's checks */
  .it > b + span { display: inline; }
  .it:last-child { border-bottom: none; }
  .it span { color: var(--muted); font-size: .9em; }
  .it .os em { font-style: normal; font-weight: 700; color: var(--fg); margin-right: .3em; }
  .proj pre.sh { font-size: .8em; }
  .proj p { font-size: .95em; }
</style>
